{"text": " So what could the night look like in 2100? That morning hasn't happened yet, but we can follow the evidence. Some places have already started protecting the dark. Since 2013, Francis told shops to switch off their window lights by one in the morning. Tucson in Arizona has had rules on outdoor lighting since 1972 to keep the sky dark for its observatories. So here's one scenario, not a fact. If the sky keeps brightening, darkness becomes something we have to protect, the way we once protected forests and coasts. A child in 2100 might see the Milky Way for the first time on a school trip in a place kept dark on purpose. And remember the bell from 1500? Cover the fire. In 2100, it might ring again. Only this time, it means cover the light.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.54, "text": " So what could the night look like in 2100?", "tokens": [50364, 407, 437, 727, 264, 1818, 574, 411, 294, 5080, 628, 30, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10327754104346559, "compression_ratio": 1.543859649122807, "no_speech_prob": 0.015703517943620682, "words": [{"word": " So", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.8347280621528625}, {"word": " what", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.36, "probability": 0.8212907910346985}, {"word": " could", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.46, "probability": 0.9152402281761169}, {"word": " the", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.58, "probability": 0.9894892573356628}, {"word": " night", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.78, "probability": 0.9847463369369507}, {"word": " look", "start": 0.78, "end": 1.14, "probability": 0.9954578876495361}, {"word": " like", "start": 1.14, "end": 1.42, "probability": 0.9988490343093872}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.42, "end": 1.68, "probability": 0.9931836724281311}, {"word": " 2100?", "start": 1.68, "end": 2.54, "probability": 0.7916874587535858}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.12, "end": 4.64, "text": " That morning hasn't happened yet,", "tokens": [50522, 663, 2446, 6132, 380, 2011, 1939, 11, 50628],